<title>PERU: Peru net reserves drop to $8.743 bln on Jan 22.</title>
<headline>Peru net reserves drop to $8.743 bln on Jan 22.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank on Friday said its net international reserves fell to $8.743 billion on January 22 from $8.819 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>The bank held reserves of $8.540 billion at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The government estimates Peru's international reserves will rise to more than $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
